# component: item
# decisions: A11Y-7, API-16, API-19, API-20, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-6, LAY-11
# hunks:
#   A11Y-7: `ItemGroup` licenses `role="listitem"` on the `Item`s inside it through context, and
#           hides the separator's rule. `role="list"` admits only `listitem` children, so upstream's
#           own composition is a CRITICAL `aria-required-children` violation as shipped.
#           Amended by MK 2026-09-24 (Regent #137 DS-68 / #138 DS-07): a row rendered as anything
#           but a `div` (a link, a button) keeps its own role, and the `listitem` moves to a
#           `<div role="listitem" data-slot="item-listitem">` wrapper. Such a control row wraps
#           its children in `TruncationFocusProvider focusable={false}`, so a truncated cell or a
#           `RelativeTime` inside it is not a nested tab stop.
#   API-16: `"use client"` is added — `useRender` calls `React.useRef` internally, so the module
#           throws on import in an RSC without the boundary (`verify-rsc-safety.mjs`).
#   API-19: `ItemDescriptionContext` + `useItemDescriptionId()` — a row that owns an accessible
#           description (Command, Select, Combobox, the three menus) provides a register function,
#           and `ItemDescription` reports its `id` to it so the row can set `aria-describedby`.
#           Outside such a row the description renders exactly as upstream's (no `id`).
#   API-20: `ItemGroupLabel`, a heading part (default `h3`, `text-xs font-medium
#           text-muted-foreground`, polymorphic through `render`). `ItemGroup` reads a label that
#           is its immediately preceding sibling after mount and points `aria-labelledby` at it;
#           a caller's own `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` always wins.
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: `outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-[3px]
#     focus-visible:ring-ring/50` is removed from `itemVariants`. `base.css` owns the one
#     `:focus-visible` outline and nothing restates it; `outline-none` would suppress it.
#   LAY-11: `line-clamp-1` is removed from `ItemTitle`. It sits on the same element as `flex`,
#     which wins the display and leaves the clamp inert — the rendered result is unchanged and
#     the class no longer claims a behaviour it does not have.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file; those hunks carry no decision of their own.
